message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Verifiable constitution: binding each principle of an LLM-agent system to an executable check"
abstract: "A domain-neutral template of ten principles (C1–C10) for software systems that embed large language model agents, in which each principle carries 'Prohibits:' clauses bound to executable verifications. A minimal example in Python and SQLite implements the clauses; every verification is exercised by planted violations, and a coverage script reports, per clause, whether the check exists and is seen failing, together with the reach declared for it. The repository also holds anonymised per-principle and per-clause data from three coverage measurements of one system and a script that reproduces the agreement between assessors."
type: software
